module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.lambda_has_no_lowered_function_value_form

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data lambda_has_no_lowered_function_value_form: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "lambda_has_no_lowered_function_value_form" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "an inline lambda (`x => body`, `(x, y) => body`, a fn literal) has no lowered function-value form in v2 body lowering outside the fold-family seam (`v2.compiler.fold_lowering`): as a call argument it is not an operand and not a value `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_value_lowered` lowers, so before gunbc#12145 the operand reader answered `f => body` with `f` and the BODY WAS DISCARDED with no diagnostic, and after it the argument refused its whole module as `body_lowering_reason_call_argument_unread`",
    "WHY CARRYING THE SHELL IS NOT THE REPAIR, MEASURED 2026-09-24. Carrying the lambda as its preserved shell under `body_lowering_reason_value_carried_unlowered` -- what `body_lower_value_lowered_or_carried` does for a field initializer -- let an undeclared name in the body reach resolve, but the resolver has no binder for a carried lambda, so the lambda's OWN PARAMETER refused as `resolve_reason_unbound_symbol` (`cav_apply(f: x => cav_undeclared)` refused at `x`), and a parenthesised lambda still refused at normalize. A refusal at the wrong atom is a wrong answer, so the carry was withdrawn and the argument stays a located refusal.",
    "EXPOSED, NOT INTRODUCED: the parent of gunbc#12145 (2de78893dfe) accepted this shape only by SILENT NARROWING -- the operand reader answered a sequence with its left element -- so the refusal on main after gunbc#12173 is a pre-existing defect made visible, not a new regression. Found by the XL-2 three-baseline identity census on gunbc#12194 (321 paths: 18 refusing at 2de78893dfe, 167 at ada85b9452, 101 after gunbc#12173).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor before gunbc#12145 (body silently discarded); mitigated since (the module refuses, loudly). CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- a lambda lowers to a function value whose parameters bind in its body and whose body's references reach the reference-site collector, or refuses at the lambda. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: body lowering has a lowered function-value form for an inline lambda on every route, whose parameters the resolver binds, so that an undeclared name in a lambda body refuses at its own atom and the lambda's parameters resolve. Sibling: `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.list_literal_has_no_lowered_form`.",
    "CLIMBED, gunbc#12210 (2026-09-24), executed on the seed interpreter. The trigger's capability landed: every function value in value position -- `x => body`, `(a, b) => body`, `fn(..) -> R { .. }` including let- and block-bodies, as a call argument, record field, field initializer or let value -- lowers through ONE producer, `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_function_value` / `body_lower_function_value_arrow`, reading its parse through the one decoder `v2.compiler.fold_lowering` `function_value_parts_optional` that the fold step also projects. It builds the Arrow a generic named fn lowers to: parameters are the domain's Named binders, which `v2.compiler.resolve` `resolve_arrow_node` scopes for the body, and each unwritten type is a fresh type parameter of that Arrow on gunbc#12217's binder edge. An unreadable shape or body refuses located (`body_lowering_reason_function_value_shape_unread` / `_body_unread`). EVIDENCE (seed-interpreted, gunbc built from the PR tree): `v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.value_position_whole_read` -- the two formerly expected-red rows (a lambda argument's parameter resolves; an undeclared name in its body refuses at its own atom), now permanent controls, plus shape controls asserting the ROUTE (binder, own fresh type parameter, body use at its authored occurrence; fn literal; let-block body lowers to Bind; record-field single-atom and record-construct bodies; `fn(_, _)`; a let-bound literal; a lambda in a match arm, the seven's `token_stream` wall). DISCRIMINATING RED: `mutation/fierce-gull-556-drop-binder` empties the domain, and the resolve control, the match-arm repro and every shape control go red. RUNG NOW: structurally guaranteed on the value-position route for the shapes above. RESIDUE, NOT THIS CLASS: emission of a generic Arrow refuses (`translate_reason_generic_arrow_not_rendered`, gunbc#12217); the builtin `fold` callee in `wave1_gate1_b1_builtin_call_resolves_end_to_end_witness_holds` is unbound at resolve without an import, restated as its own expected-red.",
    "ANONYMOUS SLOTS ARE THE SHARED MINT'S (gunbc#12210, 2026-09-26, after gunbc#12298). A function value's domain now goes through v2.std.anonymous_binder anonymous_binder_mint_domain like a named fn's, so a `_` parameter is the unauthorable `<anonymous-parameter-N>` and each fresh type parameter is spelled from its binder's minted label. The private `_` / `_'` / `_''` scheme (body_lower_function_value_binder_name, the wildcard prime counter) is deleted, and with it the second-wildcard residue this row once named: the conservation census credits minted labels (gunbc#12298).",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_function_value", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold", decl_name: "body_lower_function_value_arrow", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.fold_lowering", decl_name: "function_value_parts_optional", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
